NAME

ulibErrLog - Writes error logging information to the Xenolink log file(s)


SYNOPSIS

void  ulibErrLog(long Node, long EntryType, struct TimeDate *When, UBYTE *Data)
                     d0          d1                  a0                a1


DESCRIPTION

This function writes error logging information to the Xenolink log file(s).

This function's parameters are identical to those of ulibLog().  The only
difference is that the logging information is written only to Xenolink's
ERROR.LOG file.

For ulibErrLog(), the <Node> parameter specifies the node upon which the error
occurred; this number will be logged in brackets in the ERROR.LOG file.

If the <Node> parameter equals -1, then two dots ("..") will appear in
brackets instead; set <Node> to -1 if the error is not node specific.

This function should be used only to log important errors which require the
Sysop's immediate attention (such as an incorrect configuration file).  Less
important problems, such as aborted file transfers, are not classified as
errors, and should NOT be recorded in the ERROR.LOG file.

If any text is present in ERROR.LOG when Xenolink starts up via MT, Xenolink
will flash the screen and output a large warning message on the CLI.

<EntryType> is still configurable, but is conventionally set to '%' for this
function.


RETURNS

0 if the bit is not set.
1 if the bit is set.


SEE ALSO

ulibLog
